# ── P34.18 / ADR-178 (S0 RI-01; B-3, OD-17, OD-20) ────────────────────────────────────────────
# Commits a58fa2fa and d130b54d are the verifier-backed bulk re-key the ticket's acceptance
# criterion demands (zero handle-list entries in the repo tip's tracked files): a Part VIII
# personal-data redaction across protected records — run ledgers, pr ledgers, the LEDGER PHASE
# LOG, DEFERRALS rows, planning records, and two landed-ADR body strings — each redaction
# recorded in-place and disclosed by the dated correction note
# (docs/governance/identifier-rekey-note.md); the appended ADR notes land as conforming
# `## Status updates` sections and the re-keyed DEFERRALS rows carry `as-of` markers. Their
# verifier is docs/build/tools/handle_crawl_check.py (0 hits, counts only). Same mechanism as
# the Stage-B seeds: corrective commits whose append-only findings are sanctioned, keyed by
# prefix so no later commit can borrow them — memory_guard strips only findings *attributed*
# to a declared commit, wherever it sits in a judged range.
seed-commit a58fa2fa
seed-commit d130b54d

# ── PLAN-11B C3 contract-rewrite commit (ticket 239; recorded 2026-10-05) ─────────────────────────
# Commit 427c5efb rewrote the seven C3 skeletons (rows 272–278) into the full execute-grade
# contracts ticket 239's deliverable demands — a planned bulk rewrite, the same class as the
# Stage-B seeds and the P34.18/ADR-178 re-key. Its subject named ticket ids (`P35.14a/b`,
# `P36.3`, …), so `executed()` (B2 §7) marked the seven contracts "executing" mid-range and every
# rewritten skeleton line read as a frozen-contract edit (658 append-only findings, all attributed
# to 427c5efb — verified by the docs job's history run, run 37363207636). The rewrite is the
# sanctioned deliverable, not a correction of an executed contract; the branch rule forbids
# force-push, so the exempting declaration lands as a later commit rather than a reworded subject.
# Consequence recorded for later contexts: these seven files now read "executed" in any range that
# contains 427c5efb, and in later ranges they read executed once runs/<id>.md or a BUILD_INDEX row
# exists at base — i.e., normal BM-TICKET-04 semantics resume; subsequent edits must conform to it.
# Scope: findings attributed to 427c5efb only; no other commit borrows the exemption.
seed-commit 427c5efb

# ── P34.22a whole-tree future-date test — first-run entries ──────────────────────────────────────
# tests/unit/test_no_future_date_literals.py (P34.22a) sweeps code, data, migrations and tests for
# ISO literals later than HEAD. Real-world and scheduled values in comment-capable files carry
# `future-ok:` markers instead; the entries below cover the literals that cannot carry an inline
# marker — JSON fixtures (no comments) and values embedded inside multi-line strings — each by its
# own fixed text, each with an expiry just past the covered literal so the entry dies with the
# value it names (R5: an expired entry no longer exempts).
# The sqitch L44–52 base fixture mirrors the plan's own allow-listed change ids for the
# byte-identical C-10 assertion — same texts, same expiry as the `allow db/sqitch.plan` entries above.
allow tests/unit/fixtures/sqitch_plan_L44-52_at_p34.22a_base.txt 2026-10-19T21:00:00Z claim_assertion_bindings [camera_site_human_decisions claim_evidence ingest_run_capture access_control] 2026-10-03T12:00:00Z
allow tests/unit/fixtures/sqitch_plan_L44-52_at_p34.22a_base.txt 2026-10-19T21:00:00Z partner_org_scoped_identity_key [claim_assertion_bindings entity_identity_key] 2026-10-10T12:00:00Z
allow tests/unit/fixtures/sqitch_plan_L44-52_at_p34.22a_base.txt 2026-10-19T21:00:00Z shared_temporal_contract [partner_org_scoped_identity_key camera_site_resolution claim_assertion_bindings] 2026-10-11T00:00:00Z
allow tests/unit/fixtures/sqitch_plan_L44-52_at_p34.22a_base.txt 2026-10-19T21:00:00Z publication_dispositions [shared_temporal_contract domain_entities] 2026-10-12T00:00:00Z
allow tests/unit/fixtures/sqitch_plan_L44-52_at_p34.22a_base.txt 2026-10-19T21:00:00Z human_eval_campaign [publication_dispositions materialize_role review_campaign access_control] 2026-10-16T00:00:00Z
allow tests/unit/fixtures/sqitch_plan_L44-52_at_p34.22a_base.txt 2026-10-19T21:00:00Z disposition_decided_at_authority [publication_dispositions] 2026-09-27T14:00:00Z
allow tests/unit/fixtures/sqitch_plan_L44-52_at_p34.22a_base.txt 2026-10-19T21:00:00Z intake_storage [disposition_decided_at_authority access_control] 2026-10-18T00:00:00Z
allow tests/unit/fixtures/sqitch_plan_L44-52_at_p34.22a_base.txt 2026-10-19T21:00:00Z intake_application_bridge [intake_storage publication_dispositions entity_identity_key claim_evidence claim_assertion_bindings] 2026-10-19T00:00:00Z
allow tests/unit/fixtures/sqitch_plan_L44-52_at_p34.22a_base.txt 2026-10-19T21:00:00Z recovery_apply [intake_application_bridge] 2026-10-19T21:00:00Z
# The AR-3 windows live inside a multi-line shell string (one start/stop pair per line —
# `read -r start stop`), so no inline marker is possible; the expiry lands right after the last
# window closes.
allow ops/gcp/alerts.sh 2026-12-14T00:00:00Z AR3_WINDOWS="2026-10-06T00:00:00Z 2026-10-13T12:00:00Z
allow ops/gcp/alerts.sh 2026-12-14T00:00:00Z 2026-11-06T00:00:00Z 2026-11-13T12:00:00Z
allow ops/gcp/alerts.sh 2026-12-14T00:00:00Z 2026-12-06T00:00:00Z 2026-12-13T12:00:00Z"
allow ops/gcp/protect.sh 2026-12-14T00:00:00Z AR3_WINDOWS="2026-10-06T00:00:00Z 2026-10-13T12:00:00Z
allow ops/gcp/protect.sh 2026-12-14T00:00:00Z 2026-11-06T00:00:00Z 2026-11-13T12:00:00Z
allow ops/gcp/protect.sh 2026-12-14T00:00:00Z 2026-12-06T00:00:00Z 2026-12-13T12:00:00Z"
# Captured JSON fixtures cannot carry inline comments; these are real-world API field values
# (`"start_date"`, `"End Date"`, `"text"` — outside the R5 field-name list) whose expiries sit just
# past the covered literal, so each entry dies with the value it names (R5). The literals are
# real-world document values inside committed capture fixtures, not chain dates — the fixture-run
# regeneration wrote NEW superseding artifact dirs and kept these inputs byte-identical, so the
# entries stay until their literals pass (no removal removes a real-world value).
allow tests/connectors/fixtures/promoted/openstates_jurisdictions_p1.json 2027-02-03T00:00:00Z "start_date"
allow tests/connectors/fixtures/fema_hsgp_page1.json 2027-10-01T00:00:00Z "End Date"
allow tests/connectors/fixtures/partners/usaspending_awards.json 2027-01-01T00:00:00Z "End Date"
allow tests/acceptance/fixtures/okc_sources.json 2027-07-01T00:00:00Z 2027-06-30

# ── PLAN-11B C13 executed-flag exemption (ticket 239; recorded 2026-10-06) ────────────────────
# Commit f9c407c8 (the C13 Phase-4 split commit) named `P35.1b`/`P35.1c` in its subject, so
# `executed()` (B2 §7) marked row 291's contract "executing" mid-range and the sanctioned
# skeleton→full-contract rewrite authored by C6's f17eb537 — together with the lines the
# fix-forward 08c1840b restored verbatim to the authored text before appending the split —
# read as frozen-contract edits (148 append-only findings on
# docs/tickets/291_P35.1b__fleet-hygiene.md: 114 attributed to f17eb537, 34 to 08c1840b;
# docs-job history run 37472154666). The rewrite is PLAN-11B's deliverable — the same class
# as 427c5efb above — and the branch rule forbids force-push, so the exemption lands declared
# rather than as a reworded subject. The C13 re-scope itself lands in the contract as a
# conforming appended `> Amended 2026-10-06:` note (BM-TICKET-04); row 291a's file
# (291a_P35.1c__dispatcher-consolidation.md) is new in-range and unjudged.
# Consequence recorded for later contexts: 291's contract reads "executed" in any range that
# contains f9c407c8 — subsequent edits must conform to BM-TICKET-04 — and 291a's reads the
# same once runs/P35.1c.md or a BUILD_INDEX row exists at base.
# Scope: findings attributed to f17eb537 and 08c1840b only; no other commit borrows the
# exemption.
seed-commit f17eb537
seed-commit 08c1840b

